  ($$forearm_mappings_v1$$, $$cat-140:forearm.ecu$$, $$cat-140$$, $$forearm.ecu$$, $$wrist.extension$$, $$direct$$, $$dynamic$$, $$anatomy$$, $$individual$$, false, $$A reverse wrist curl is built on wrist extension, one of the extensor carpi ulnaris's main actions; the wrist moves through range against the load.$$, $$reviewed$$, $$same$$),
  ($$forearm_mappings_v1$$, $$cat-140:forearm.ed$$, $$cat-140$$, $$forearm.ed$$, $$wrist.extension$$, $$contributing$$, $$dynamic$$, $$anatomy$$, $$individual$$, false, $$The extensor digitorum assists wrist extension, but its main job is straightening the fingers, which stay closed on the bar; it is contributing, not direct. This is wrist extension, not finger extension.$$, $$reviewed$$, $$same$$),
