  ($$forearm_mappings_v1$$, $$cat-379:forearm.br$$, $$cat-379$$, $$forearm.br$$, $$elbow.flexion$$, $$contributing$$, $$dynamic$$, $$anatomy$$, $$individual$$, false, $$The elbows bend under load in a row, pulldown or pull-up, and the brachioradialis is an elbow flexor, so it helps move the load through range. Its share changes with hand position (M1), and the back muscles are the target, so it is contributing, never direct.$$, $$reviewed$$, $$same$$),
