  ($$forearm_mappings_v1$$, $$cat-402:forearm.fds$$, $$cat-402$$, $$forearm.fds$$, $$fingers.pip_flexion$$, $$direct$$, $$dynamic$$, $$anatomy$$, $$shared$$, false, $$Closing the gripper bends the fingers against the spring, so the finger flexors move through range: direct, dynamic work, shared between FDS and FDP.$$, $$reviewed$$, $$same$$),
  ($$forearm_mappings_v1$$, $$cat-403:forearm.fdp$$, $$cat-403$$, $$forearm.fdp$$, $$fingers.dip_flexion$$, $$direct$$, $$isometric$$, $$anatomy$$, $$shared$$, false, $$Holding on is the purpose of the set, so the finger flexors are the direct target, working isometrically for the time logged. FDS and FDP share the work; nothing in a whole-hand grip separates them (S3, S8). Straps do not apply to a gripper.$$, $$reviewed$$, $$same$$),
