  ($$forearm_mappings_v1$$, $$cat-414:forearm.apl$$, $$cat-414$$, $$forearm.apl$$, $$thumb.cmc_abduction$$, $$direct$$, $$dynamic$$, $$anatomy$$, $$individual$$, false, $$Moving the thumb away from the index finger at its base against a band is thumb abduction, the abductor pollicis longus's action. The short abductor in the hand also works, but hand muscles are not forearm muscles and are not credited here.$$, $$reviewed$$, $$same$$),
  ($$forearm_mappings_v1$$, $$cat-415:forearm.ecrb$$, $$cat-415$$, $$forearm.ecrb$$, $$wrist.extension$$, $$direct$$, $$dynamic$$, $$anatomy$$, $$individual$$, false, $$Winding by rolling the top of the roller toward you, palms down is a series of wrist extensions against the hanging weight, one of this muscle's main actions: direct, dynamic work.$$, $$reviewed$$, $$same$$),
